  "id": "COMPOUND:11699 - PROTEIN:4665",
  "verbalization": "Anethole trithione appears to interact with Ephrin type-A receptor 3 through a multi-step mechanism involving a common intermediate compound, (1S,2S,5R,6R,7S,8S,11S)-7-hydroxy-5-(hydroxymethyl)-11-[(2R)-1-hydroxypropan-2-yl]-6-methyl-9-oxatricyclo[6.2.1.02,6]undecan-10-one. This compound is identified as a target of Anethole trithione and is also a target of MAP kinase-activated protein kinase 5, suggesting that Anethole trithione may act through a pathway that involves the activation of this intermediate compound. The evidence suggests that Anethole trithione may inhibit Ephrin type-A receptor 3 by first modulating the activity of this intermediate compound, which in turn affects the receptor. The presence of multiple paths with similar scores indicates a consistent and robust relationship between Anethole trithione and Ephrin type-A receptor 3, supporting a mechanistic link that is both biologically plausible and consistent across different targets. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Anethole trithione to exert its effects through a complex network of molecular interactions involving this intermediate compound and its downstream targets.",
